WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
Speaker 1: Welcome back to the David Pakman&nbsp;
show. I am Ferron cousins from Ring of Fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:11.040
once again filling in for David. You&nbsp;
know, one of the things that we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.920
talked about a lot with regard to the&nbsp;
January six hearing is whether or not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:24.000
any of these televised hearings are going to have&nbsp;
any kind of impact on the 2022 midterm elections.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:32.720
And according to former Tea Party Republican Joe&nbsp;
Walsh, who tweeted out on Thursday, no, they will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:38.480
have absolutely no impact. Here is Joe Walsh's&nbsp;
tweet. Twitter world may not understand this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:44.000
but January six and these hearings won't make&nbsp;
any difference in the midterms. The hearings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.760
are important and necessary, but they&nbsp;
will have zero impact this November.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:59.120
It's kind of a bummer, right? I mean, way to come&nbsp;
along and ruin everybody's mood, their captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:08.400
buzzkill. But at the same time, I don't completely&nbsp;
disagree with them. I do think for the most part,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:14.000
and I'm struggling to say that because I don't&nbsp;
know how much I believe him or agree with him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:21.840
But I do think he's right. If these things do&nbsp;
end up having an impact on the 2022 midterms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:30.080
I don't think it's going to be a hugely measurable&nbsp;
impact. Right. It may affect like a couple races,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:38.480
but I don't think it's going to affect enough of&nbsp;
them to stop what we all see as likely coming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:43.440
which, of course, is Republicans taking back the&nbsp;
House. I don't see it doing that. I don't see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:50.320
enough momentum with this. I don't see enough,&nbsp;
you know, tying it in to the other Republicans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:56.240
because the hearings, of course, are all really&nbsp;
about Donald Trump and his administration. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:00.640
we've, you know, identified several Republican&nbsp;
members of Congress that were involved.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:07.120
But even if we took out each and every one of&nbsp;
those people in the elections, Republicans would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:12.960
still be poised to take back the House. So that&nbsp;
is why I do, again, kind of agree with what Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:22.880
Walsh has to say. But then the other. But is the&nbsp;
poll numbers right? The poll numbers out there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.160
are kind of contradicting it, at least right now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:32.880
Here's what they tell us. Nearly two thirds&nbsp;
of U.S. adults believe the January six,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:39.360
2021 riot at the Capitol was planned, according&nbsp;
to a new Quinnipiac poll. Poll found that 64% of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:45.120
respondents believe the attack was planned&nbsp;
and 30% believed it was spontaneous. Okay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:51.520
so it's influencing public opinion, which is&nbsp;
great. I mean, that's the whole point of all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:56.560
this. We want to influence public opinion, but&nbsp;
not because we're trying to brainwash them or,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:01.120
you know, push them into any kind of political&nbsp;
ideology. But because we want to influence their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:06.000
opinion on the people who perpetrated these acts.&nbsp;
And there is a big difference between those two.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.480
This is not a partizan political committee, as&nbsp;
the Republicans would like to have you believe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:18.800
This is in fact a fact finding mission. And so&nbsp;
far, a lot of the facts that they found have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:29.280
been very bad for the Republican Party. So the&nbsp;
question is, could it have an impact on the 2022&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:38.560
midterms in a meaningful way? And the answer is&nbsp;
possibly in order. However, for that to happen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:44.160
the committee's work would have to focus&nbsp;
more on the Republican Party as a whole.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:50.560
You know, not just paint Donald Trump and Giuliani&nbsp;
and some of these other weird little characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:57.120
out there. As, you know, the only people they&nbsp;
would have to come back in and tie it all in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:05.040
saying this, folks, is who the current Republican&nbsp;
Party is. And that's not the job of the committee.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:13.840
That's the job of the Democratic Party.&nbsp;
And that's where that disconnect exists.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:20.640
The January six committee has done great work. I&nbsp;
was skeptical of them at first. Didn't think they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:24.720
could pull it off. They have they have proven&nbsp;
me wrong and I am grateful to them for it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:31.360
But now is the time for the Democratic Party&nbsp;
to step up because, yes, these hearings are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:37.440
impactful. Yes, they are changing public opinion.&nbsp;
But the committee is not going to sit there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.160
especially with Republican like Liz Cheney&nbsp;
sitting on there and say this is who all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:46.240
Republicans are. They're not going to do&nbsp;
that. And they shouldn't do that either.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:52.000
They kind of should, but they can't. I understand.&nbsp;
They absolutely cannot, because you will start to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:59.680
turn off people. What the Democratic Party could&nbsp;
do should have already been doing. It's turning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:05.840
some of this into ads. Ads running on national&nbsp;
television channels all across the country.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:17.280
But they're not. The messaging from the&nbsp;
Democratic Party needs to be that this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:23.840
who the Republicans are. Not this is who&nbsp;
Trump is not. This is who Jim Jordan is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:33.600
This is who they all are. Every one of them. Yes.&nbsp;
Use that language. Yes. I don't care if it makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:40.640
Liz Cheney or Adam Kinzinger or sitting on that&nbsp;
committee angry. This is your opportunity. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:44.560
public is paying attention to these hearings.&nbsp;
Millions of people have already tuned in.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:51.840
The polls are shifting in pretty significant&nbsp;
ways. I mean, rather shocking ways, if you ask me.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.040 --> 00:06:00.800
So seize that moment, jump on that opportunity,&nbsp;
and put it in ads. Put it in people's faces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:06.960
every day. Tie every single Republican&nbsp;
candidate out there back to these people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:12.240
Because even if they didn't&nbsp;
participate, they still vote with them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.960
Hell, a lot of the candidates out there running&nbsp;
for office actually support what happened that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:23.920
day. They still support Donald Trump. That's why&nbsp;
you do have candidates, by the way, like Dr. Oz,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:29.680
who have now shifted their messaging to stop&nbsp;
mentioning Trump as much. And, you know, moving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:35.600
back on to just just the issues, folks, don't let&nbsp;
them do that. Don't let them get the upper hand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:42.480
Tie every Republican in the country to&nbsp;
everything this committee has found. You do that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:48.560
you may have a pretty significant impact on the&nbsp;
midterms. But if the Democratic Party is sitting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:52.640
there waiting for the January six committee to&nbsp;
do this themselves, it ain't going to happen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:57.840
That is not the job of this committee. And&nbsp;
if they attempted to do that, they're going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:04.800
to lose all the credibility that they have. This&nbsp;
is on the Democratic Party. They could do this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:14.000
They should do this. But if history is&nbsp;
any indicator, they won't be doing that.

